==Evolution==
Evolves into '''NEK-0 Sky Fortress''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''NEK-02 Air Citadel''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''NEK-03 Cloud Emperor''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mighty Bomburr is an excellent support unit against Zombies, especially hordes. Its [[Knockback|Knockback]] ability and relatively fast attack rate can consistently regain ground versus Zombies, allowing [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] heavy hitters like [[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|Rock Revengers]] or [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Drednot]] to wipe them out with ease. It can even stop slow Zombies from ever attacking your [[Cat Base]], sapping their health over time all by itself! This is notable in [[The Infected King]], where it easily stunlocks [[Big Sal]], preventing him from even advancing.

It has all necessary general stats, those being survivability, DPS, and range, everything you could ever ask for in a generalist! However, while these stats are good, there are units with better DPS than them. They aren't likely to be your definite generalist unit, even though they're great in nearly every regard. Otherwise, it simply boils down to the higher cost and recharge time, making them tedious in stages where these aspects matter most.

==='''True Form'''===
Sadly, all the Citadel crew gets is extra health, but survivability was already a very strong point of their previous forms, fixing nothing and adding unnecessary improvements. It does make them more comfortable to use, but only invest in this for their Talents and/or Ultra Form.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
NEK-03 Cloud Emperor gains several buffs which transform them into both a better generalist DPS and specialist crowd-controller.

Most notable is the addition of an [[Omni Strike]] with decent forward pierce, which makes them even more comfortable to use against Zombies, being far less likely of missing an attack due to burrowing. This works in tandem with [[Explosion]], granting them an enormous coverage of up to 725 range if it activates. Their DPS is also improved dramatically by this ability, shooting up to an average of ''13,700'', and ''20,500'' if Strengthened from Talents. Although inconsistent at a 50/50 proc chance, their attack rate is fast enough to cover for this.

[[Omni Strike|Sage Slayer]] has one primary target: [[Oldstrich]], which they're capable of countering very well in many of its appearances. But more than that, the health (2x) and damage (1.2x) increase provided by this ability makes them a viable counter against many Sages as a generalist attacker. Enemies such as [[Techn-Old Hyena]], [[Doctor K.O.]], [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], and even [[Sage of Mind Soractes]] are all easily outranged by this Emperor. And others that still manage to target them (like [[Tarsiriel]]) will have to get through their 332,800 effective HP.

Overall, Bomburr's Ultra Form grants them enough buffs to actually be a relevant and decently viable unit. However, the existence of many other anti-Zombie Ubers from the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] banner as well as the presence of other, more powerful generalists means that investing your precious Dark Catseyes as well as NP for the Strengthen Talent should be done at your own discretion after considering all of your options.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Freeze Resist]]''' isn't going to help aside from [[Henry]], so it is best not to invest in it.

With the '''[[Strengthen]]''' ability, it has fixed one of his previous flaws, low DPS. Thankfully, it is triggered at 43% or lower health, meaning NEK-02 Air Citadel will still have a decent amount of health to be used. This, provided with their damage Talent, can make them a monster! In Ultra Form, this Talent is even more recommended.

His '''Health''' and '''Attack Buff''' Talents can help him in many situations, but it's usually better to go the [[Catseye]] route and boost them via XP to save NP.

'''[[Immune to Toxic|Toxic Immune]]''' helps them become an anti-Toxic attacker, as most enemies with the Toxic ability has low damage per hit, meaning they can trigger their Strengthen faster. As previously mentioned, their decent generalist values help with Toxic stages, countering [[Gobble]]s and [[Zollow]]s decently. In Ultra Form, it gains further relevance against Oldstrich.

'''[[Soulstrike]]''' is an excellent Talent. Thanks to this unit's fast attack rate and Knockback ability, it can easily clear out lesser zombies and constantly push back stronger ones as long as they are not immune.

